1
00:03:58,572 --> 00:04:00,032
I'll find you later.

2
00:04:02,772 --> 00:04:04,022
It's not safe.

3
00:04:07,392 --> 00:04:09,152
Let me send some men with you.

4
00:04:13,032 --> 00:04:14,372
I'm going alone.

5
00:05:00,362 --> 00:05:02,262
In the name of the one true queen,

6
00:05:02,262 --> 00:05:03,992
Daenerys Targaryen,

7
00:05:04,722 --> 00:05:06,532
I sentence you to die.

8
00:05:07,382 --> 00:05:08,492
Grey Worm!

9
00:05:15,742 --> 00:05:16,932
It's over.

10
00:05:17,722 --> 00:05:19,462
These men are prisoners.

11
00:05:19,522 --> 00:05:21,932
It is not over until the queen's enemies are defeated.

12
00:05:21,932 --> 00:05:24,152
How much more defeated do you want them to be?

13
00:05:24,152 --> 00:05:26,422
- They're on their knees. - They are breathing.

14
00:05:27,292 --> 00:05:29,432
Look around you, friend. We won.

15
00:05:29,432 --> 00:05:31,942
I obey my queen's commands, not yours.

16
00:05:31,942 --> 00:05:33,722
And what are the queen's commands?

17
00:05:35,382 --> 00:05:38,332
"Kill all who follow Cersei Lannister."

18
00:05:39,332 --> 00:05:40,742
These are free men.

19
00:05:41,772 --> 00:05:43,252
They chose to fight for her.

20
00:05:46,532 --> 00:05:49,342
Easy, men. Easy! Easy.

21
00:05:58,902 --> 00:05:59,842
Jon.

22
00:06:02,682 --> 00:06:04,312
We should speak with the queen.

23
00:14:35,972 --> 00:14:37,362
Torgo Nudho.

24
00:17:19,562 --> 00:17:21,122
You freed your brother.

25
00:17:22,282 --> 00:17:23,842
You committed treason.

26
00:17:25,602 --> 00:17:27,512
I freed my brother.

27
00:17:30,742 --> 00:17:32,922
And you slaughtered a city.

28
00:19:27,102 --> 00:19:28,432
What are you doing here?

29
00:19:33,442 --> 00:19:34,522
What happened?

30
00:19:34,922 --> 00:19:36,202
I came to kill Cersei.

31
00:19:37,942 --> 00:19:39,512
Your queen got there first.

32
00:19:44,172 --> 00:19:45,892
She's everyone's queen now.

33
00:19:46,682 --> 00:19:47,982
Try telling Sansa.

34
00:19:55,902 --> 00:19:57,422
Wait for me outside the city gates.

35
00:19:57,422 --> 00:19:58,762
- I'll come find you. - Jon.

36
00:20:01,342 --> 00:20:02,562
She knows who you are.

37
00:20:04,052 --> 00:20:05,172
Who you really are.

38
00:20:06,202 --> 00:20:07,792
You'll always be a threat to her.

39
00:20:10,442 --> 00:20:12,162
And I know a killer when I see one.

40
00:20:45,332 --> 00:20:46,752
Did you bring any wine?

41
00:20:48,312 --> 00:20:49,022
No.

42
00:20:52,562 --> 00:20:53,272
Well...

43
00:20:55,622 --> 00:20:57,712
thank you for coming to see me.

44
00:20:59,002 --> 00:21:01,882
Our queen doesn't keep prisoners for long.

45
00:21:03,642 --> 00:21:06,662
I suppose there's a crude kind of justice.

46
00:21:08,572 --> 00:21:11,442
I betrayed my closest friend and watched him burn.

47
00:21:12,542 --> 00:21:15,372
Now Varys's ashes can tell my ashes:

48
00:21:15,482 --> 00:21:17,882
"See, I told you."

49
00:21:22,752 --> 00:21:24,202
It just occurred to me.

50
00:21:24,852 --> 00:21:27,762
I'm talking to the only man alive who knows where I'm going.

51
00:21:29,982 --> 00:21:32,112
So is there life after death?

52
00:21:35,592 --> 00:21:36,812
Not that I've seen.

53
00:21:38,432 --> 00:21:39,642
I should be thankful.

54
00:21:40,912 --> 00:21:42,992
Oblivion is the best I could hope for.

55
00:21:44,792 --> 00:21:46,322
I strangled my lover.

56
00:21:47,372 --> 00:21:49,502
I shot my own father with a crossbow.

57
00:21:49,502 --> 00:21:50,612
I betrayed my queen.

58
00:21:50,612 --> 00:21:52,102
- You didn't. - I did.

59
00:21:54,052 --> 00:21:55,052
And I'd do it again,

60
00:21:55,052 --> 00:21:56,862
now that I've seen what I've seen.

61
00:21:58,602 --> 00:22:00,012
I chose my fate.

62
00:22:00,772 --> 00:22:02,822
The people of King's Landing did not.

63
00:22:05,852 --> 00:22:07,852
I can't justify what happened.

64
00:22:09,672 --> 00:22:10,772
I won't try.

65
00:22:14,142 --> 00:22:16,762
- But the war is over now. - Is it?

66
00:22:19,342 --> 00:22:21,682
When you heard her talking to her soldiers,

67
00:22:22,462 --> 00:22:25,312
did she sound like someone who's done fighting?

68
00:22:33,582 --> 00:22:36,222
She liberated the people of Slaver's Bay.

69
00:22:36,652 --> 00:22:39,052
She liberated the people of King's Landing.

70
00:22:39,762 --> 00:22:41,562
And she'll go on liberating

71
00:22:41,752 --> 00:22:43,852
until the people of the world are free...

72
00:22:44,832 --> 00:22:46,522
and she rules them all.

73
00:22:46,522 --> 00:22:48,812
And you've been by her side, counseling her.

74
00:22:49,582 --> 00:22:50,652
Until today.

75
00:22:52,622 --> 00:22:53,782
Until today.

76
00:22:57,422 --> 00:22:58,582
Varys was right.

77
00:22:59,482 --> 00:23:00,472
I was wrong.

78
00:23:01,582 --> 00:23:03,922
It was vanity to think I could guide her.

79
00:23:04,482 --> 00:23:06,922
Our queen's nature is fire and blood.

80
00:23:07,132 --> 00:23:09,282
You think our house words are stamped on our bodies

81
00:23:09,282 --> 00:23:11,152
when we're born and that's who we are?

82
00:23:11,572 --> 00:23:13,722
Then I'd be fire and blood too.

83
00:23:15,612 --> 00:23:16,652
She's not her father,

84
00:23:16,662 --> 00:23:18,572
no more than you're Tywin Lannister.

85
00:23:18,582 --> 00:23:23,282
My father was an evil man. My sister was an evil woman.

86
00:23:23,762 --> 00:23:26,962
Pile up all the bodies of all the people they ever killed,

87
00:23:27,312 --> 00:23:28,722
there still won't be half as many

88
00:23:28,722 --> 00:23:31,732
as our beautiful queen slaughtered in a single day.

89
00:23:31,732 --> 00:23:32,892
Cersei left her no choice.

90
00:23:32,892 --> 00:23:35,302
The moment the gates fell, the battle was over.

91
00:23:35,302 --> 00:23:37,262
She saw her friend beheaded.

92
00:23:37,662 --> 00:23:39,272
She saw her dragon shot out of the sky.

93
00:23:39,272 --> 00:23:41,692
And she burned down a city for it.

94
00:23:42,122 --> 00:23:43,862
Ah, it's easy to judge when you're standing

95
00:23:43,862 --> 00:23:45,272
far from the battlefield.

96
00:23:45,272 --> 00:23:46,422
Would you have done it?

97
00:23:48,332 --> 00:23:49,092
What?

98
00:23:51,232 --> 00:23:53,962
You've been up there, on a dragon's back.

99
00:23:53,962 --> 00:23:55,432
You've had that power.

100
00:23:55,442 --> 00:23:57,452
Would you have burned the city down?

101
00:24:01,072 --> 00:24:01,972
I don't know.

102
00:24:03,282 --> 00:24:04,672
Yes, you do.

103
00:24:06,782 --> 00:24:09,712
You won't say because you don't want to betray her...

104
00:24:11,612 --> 00:24:12,912
but you know.

105
00:24:21,382 --> 00:24:23,132
What's it matter what I'd do?

106
00:24:23,992 --> 00:24:26,622
It matters more than anything.

107
00:24:31,222 --> 00:24:33,872
When she murdered the slavers of Astapor,

108
00:24:35,242 --> 00:24:37,462
I'm sure no one but the slavers complained.

109
00:24:37,462 --> 00:24:39,392
After all, they were evil men.

110
00:24:41,332 --> 00:24:44,552
When she crucified hundreds of Meereenese nobles,

111
00:24:44,902 --> 00:24:46,012
who could argue?

112
00:24:46,012 --> 00:24:47,432
They were evil men.

113
00:24:48,772 --> 00:24:51,822
The Dothraki khals she burned alive?

114
00:24:52,432 --> 00:24:54,502
They would have done worse to her.

115
00:24:56,512 --> 00:25:00,382
Everywhere she goes, evil men die

116
00:25:00,702 --> 00:25:02,892
and we cheer her for it.

117
00:25:04,272 --> 00:25:05,822
And she grows more powerful

118
00:25:05,822 --> 00:25:09,372
and more sure that she is good and right.

119
00:25:14,552 --> 00:25:16,002
She believes her destiny

120
00:25:16,002 --> 00:25:18,832
is to build a better world for everyone.

121
00:25:19,342 --> 00:25:20,512
If you believed that...

122
00:25:22,552 --> 00:25:23,722
if you truly believed it,

123
00:25:23,722 --> 00:25:24,902
wouldn't you kill

124
00:25:24,902 --> 00:25:27,132
whoever stood between you and paradise?

125
00:25:59,222 --> 00:26:00,672
I know you love her.

126
00:26:06,572 --> 00:26:07,882
I love her too.

127
00:26:12,242 --> 00:26:15,782
Not as successfully as you.

128
00:26:18,652 --> 00:26:23,092
But I believed in her with all my heart.

129
00:26:31,072 --> 00:26:34,252
Love is more powerful than reason.

130
00:26:36,702 --> 00:26:38,182
We all know that.

131
00:26:38,842 --> 00:26:40,132
Look at my brother.

132
00:26:45,722 --> 00:26:47,552
"Love is the death of duty."

133
00:26:53,882 --> 00:26:55,322
You just came up with that?

134
00:27:01,512 --> 00:27:04,212
Maester Aemon said it a long time ago.

135
00:27:09,972 --> 00:27:14,442
Sometimes duty is the death of love.

136
00:27:19,822 --> 00:27:23,412
You are the shield that guards the realms of men.

137
00:27:24,102 --> 00:27:26,622
And you've always tried to do the right thing.

138
00:27:26,702 --> 00:27:30,922
No matter the cost, you've tried to protect people.

139
00:27:33,782 --> 00:27:36,362
Who is the greatest threat to the people now?

140
00:27:44,372 --> 00:27:46,742
It's a terrible thing I'm asking.

141
00:27:48,362 --> 00:27:50,192
It's also the right thing.

142
00:27:52,752 --> 00:27:56,072
Do you think I'm the last man she'll execute?

143
00:27:58,232 --> 00:28:00,602
Who is more dangerous than the rightful

144
00:28:00,602 --> 00:28:02,412
heir to the Iron Throne?

145
00:28:15,882 --> 00:28:18,502
That's her decision. She is the queen.

146
00:28:27,482 --> 00:28:29,142
I'm sorry it came to this.

147
00:28:41,192 --> 00:28:42,632
And your sisters?

148
00:28:45,112 --> 00:28:47,252
Do you see them bending the knee?

149
00:28:51,692 --> 00:28:53,752
My sisters will be loyal to the throne.

150
00:28:53,752 --> 00:28:56,482
Why do you think Sansa told me the truth about you?

151
00:28:57,372 --> 00:28:59,312
Because she doesn't want Dany to be queen.

152
00:28:59,312 --> 00:29:01,492
- She doesn't get to choose. - No.

153
00:29:02,282 --> 00:29:03,552
But you do.

154
00:29:05,052 --> 00:29:15,052
分析，谁会活到最后？
上知乎搜索「权游谁会死」，给出你的神预测

155
00:29:05,372 --> 00:29:07,212
And you have to choose now.

156
00:33:07,632 --> 00:33:09,612
When I was a girl, my brother told me

157
00:33:09,612 --> 00:33:13,482
it was made with 1000 swords from Aegon's fallen enemies.

158
00:33:16,552 --> 00:33:18,572
What do 1000 swords look like

159
00:33:18,572 --> 00:33:21,082
in the mind of a little girl who can't count to 20?

160
00:33:22,682 --> 00:33:26,092
I imagined a mountain of swords too high to climb.

161
00:33:26,482 --> 00:33:28,182
So many fallen enemies,

162
00:33:28,192 --> 00:33:30,412
you could only see the soles of Aegon's feet.

163
00:33:30,412 --> 00:33:33,132
I saw them executing Lannister prisoners in the street.

164
00:33:34,652 --> 00:33:36,632
They said they were acting on your orders.

165
00:33:37,822 --> 00:33:39,862
- It was necessary. - Necessary?

166
00:33:40,662 --> 00:33:42,002
Have you been down there?

167
00:33:42,272 --> 00:33:43,272
Have you seen?

168
00:33:43,692 --> 00:33:46,932
Children, little children, burned!

169
00:33:49,382 --> 00:33:51,772
I tried to make peace with Cersei.

170
00:33:53,242 --> 00:33:56,442
She used their innocence as a weapon against me.

171
00:33:57,382 --> 00:33:58,652
She thought it would cripple me.

172
00:33:58,652 --> 00:33:59,572
And Tyrion?

173
00:34:03,952 --> 00:34:06,382
He conspired behind my back with my enemies.

174
00:34:07,712 --> 00:34:09,962
How have you treated people who've done the same to you,

175
00:34:10,322 --> 00:34:12,272
even when it broke your heart?

176
00:34:15,302 --> 00:34:16,122
Forgive him.

177
00:34:19,282 --> 00:34:20,962
- I can't. - You can.

178
00:34:22,612 --> 00:34:24,012
You can forgive all of them,

179
00:34:24,012 --> 00:34:26,012
make them see they made a mistake.

180
00:34:26,702 --> 00:34:28,062
Make them understand.

181
00:34:33,242 --> 00:34:34,542
Please, Dany.

182
00:34:38,562 --> 00:34:40,712
We can't hide behind small mercies.

183
00:34:42,342 --> 00:34:44,022
The world we need

184
00:34:44,622 --> 00:34:47,532
won't be built by men loyal to the world we have.

185
00:34:47,542 --> 00:34:51,212
The world we need is a world of mercy. It has to be.

186
00:34:51,442 --> 00:34:52,672
And it will be.

187
00:34:56,032 --> 00:35:00,852
It's not easy to see something that's never been before.

188
00:35:03,282 --> 00:35:05,002
A good world.

189
00:35:05,992 --> 00:35:06,962
How do you know?

190
00:35:09,712 --> 00:35:11,202
How do you know it'll be good?

191
00:35:11,912 --> 00:35:13,552
Because I know what is good.

192
00:35:15,222 --> 00:35:16,322
And so do you.

193
00:35:16,322 --> 00:35:18,252
- I don't. - You do.

194
00:35:18,772 --> 00:35:20,612
You do. You've always known.

195
00:35:24,282 --> 00:35:25,652
What about everyone else?

196
00:35:28,092 --> 00:35:30,462
All the other people who think they know what's good.

197
00:35:33,522 --> 00:35:35,122
They don't get to choose.

198
00:35:41,392 --> 00:35:42,432
Be with me.

199
00:35:44,112 --> 00:35:46,202
Build the new world with me.

200
00:35:46,302 --> 00:35:47,992
This is our reason.

201
00:35:48,962 --> 00:35:50,472
It has been from the beginning,

202
00:35:50,472 --> 00:35:53,392
since you were a little boy with a bastard's name

203
00:35:53,962 --> 00:35:56,832
and I was a little girl who couldn't count to 20.

204
00:35:58,052 --> 00:35:59,832
We do it together.

205
00:36:01,942 --> 00:36:04,752
We break the wheel together.

206
00:36:07,952 --> 00:36:09,292
You are my queen.

207
00:36:10,962 --> 00:36:13,832
Now, and always.

208
00:43:36,352 --> 00:43:37,452
Where's Jon?

209
00:43:38,472 --> 00:43:40,952
- He is our prisoner. - So is Lord Tyrion.

210
00:43:40,952 --> 00:43:42,902
They were both to be brought to this gathering.

211
00:43:43,132 --> 00:43:45,292
We will decide what we do with our prisoners.

212
00:43:46,012 --> 00:43:47,372
This is our city now.

213
00:43:47,822 --> 00:43:50,122
If you look outside the walls of your city,

214
00:43:50,122 --> 00:43:52,742
you'll find thousands of Northmen who will explain to you

215
00:43:52,752 --> 00:43:56,472
why harming Jon Snow is not in your interest.

216
00:43:56,472 --> 00:43:58,042
And you will find thousands of Unsullied

217
00:43:58,042 --> 00:43:59,352
who believe that it is.

218
00:43:59,532 --> 00:44:01,492
Some of you may be quick to forgive.

219
00:44:02,192 --> 00:44:03,742
The Ironborn are not.

220
00:44:04,372 --> 00:44:06,352
I swore to follow Daenerys Targaryen.

221
00:44:06,352 --> 00:44:07,802
You swore to follow a tyrant.

222
00:44:07,802 --> 00:44:09,642
She freed us from a tyrant.

223
00:44:10,032 --> 00:44:11,622
Cersei is gone because of her,

224
00:44:11,622 --> 00:44:13,762
and Jon Snow put a knife in her heart.

225
00:44:14,172 --> 00:44:16,592
Let the Unsullied give him what he deserves.

226
00:44:16,592 --> 00:44:18,182
Say another word about killing my brother

227
00:44:18,182 --> 00:44:19,652
and I'll cut your throat.

228
00:44:19,652 --> 00:44:21,112
Friends, please.

229
00:44:23,372 --> 00:44:25,622
We've been cutting each other's throats long enough.

230
00:44:26,592 --> 00:44:29,392
Torgo Nudho. Am I saying that properly?

231
00:44:33,022 --> 00:44:34,592
If it weren't for you and your men,

232
00:44:34,592 --> 00:44:36,522
we would've lost the war with the dead.

233
00:44:37,142 --> 00:44:39,642
This country owes you a debt it can never repay,

234
00:44:39,642 --> 00:44:41,562
but let us try.

235
00:44:42,322 --> 00:44:43,702
There is land in the Reach.

236
00:44:43,712 --> 00:44:44,772
Good land.

237
00:44:44,832 --> 00:44:46,712
The people that used to live there are gone.

238
00:44:47,652 --> 00:44:49,502
Make it your own. Start your own house

239
00:44:49,502 --> 00:44:51,342
with the Unsullied as your bannermen.

240
00:44:52,382 --> 00:44:53,992
We've had enough war.

241
00:44:53,992 --> 00:44:56,222
Thousands of you, thousands of them.

242
00:44:56,432 --> 00:44:57,742
You know how it ends.

243
00:44:58,372 --> 00:45:00,142
We need to find a better way.

244
00:45:00,282 --> 00:45:01,812
We do not need payment.

245
00:45:02,752 --> 00:45:04,032
We need justice.

246
00:45:05,522 --> 00:45:07,182
Jon Snow cannot go free.

247
00:45:10,422 --> 00:45:12,192
It's not for you to decide.

248
00:45:12,192 --> 00:45:13,752
You are not here to speak!

249
00:45:15,002 --> 00:45:17,032
Everyone has heard enough words from you.

250
00:45:19,472 --> 00:45:20,562
You're right.

251
00:45:21,342 --> 00:45:23,802
And no one's any better for it.

252
00:45:25,322 --> 00:45:27,872
But it's not for you to decide.

253
00:45:29,142 --> 00:45:30,832
Jon committed his crime here.

254
00:45:31,822 --> 00:45:34,192
His fate is for our king to decide.

255
00:45:34,982 --> 00:45:36,262
Or our queen.

256
00:45:36,542 --> 00:45:38,692
We don't have a king or queen.

257
00:45:39,872 --> 00:45:42,492
You're the most powerful people in Westeros.

258
00:45:45,362 --> 00:45:46,372
Choose one.

259
00:45:56,602 --> 00:45:57,822
Make your choice, then.

260
00:46:20,872 --> 00:46:22,332
My lords and ladies...

261
00:46:26,052 --> 00:46:29,692
I suppose this is the most important moment of our lives.

262
00:46:30,452 --> 00:46:32,652
What we decide today will reverberate

263
00:46:32,652 --> 00:46:34,232
through the annals of history.

264
00:46:34,992 --> 00:46:36,352
I stand before you

265
00:46:36,932 --> 00:46:39,172
as one of the senior lords in the country.

266
00:46:40,532 --> 00:46:42,172
A veteran of two wars.

267
00:46:43,582 --> 00:46:44,562
And I like to think my experience

268
00:46:44,562 --> 00:46:48,772
has led to some small skill in statecraft

269
00:46:49,072 --> 00:46:50,282
- and underst-- - Uncle?

270
00:46:53,282 --> 00:46:54,272
Please sit.

271
00:47:26,282 --> 00:47:28,322
Well, we have to choose someone.

272
00:47:30,122 --> 00:47:31,342
Why just us?

273
00:47:39,032 --> 00:47:41,302
We represent all the great houses,

274
00:47:41,332 --> 00:47:42,742
but whomever we choose,

275
00:47:42,822 --> 00:47:45,052
they won't just rule over lords and ladies.

276
00:47:46,252 --> 00:47:49,552
Maybe the decision about what's best for everyone

277
00:47:49,552 --> 00:47:50,672
should be left to...

278
00:47:51,822 --> 00:47:53,742
well, everyone.

279
00:48:08,272 --> 00:48:10,662
Maybe we should give the dogs a vote as well.

280
00:48:10,852 --> 00:48:12,572
I'll ask my horse.

281
00:48:21,982 --> 00:48:23,512
I suppose you want the crown.

282
00:48:24,752 --> 00:48:25,612
Me?

283
00:48:26,392 --> 00:48:27,392
The Imp?

284
00:48:29,582 --> 00:48:32,072
Half the people hate me for serving Daenerys,

285
00:48:32,072 --> 00:48:34,392
the other half hate me for betraying her.

286
00:48:36,262 --> 00:48:39,272
- Can't think of a worse choice. - Who, then?

287
00:48:46,322 --> 00:48:50,222
I've had nothing to do but think these past few weeks.

288
00:48:52,032 --> 00:48:53,782
About our bloody history.

289
00:48:55,852 --> 00:48:57,812
About the mistakes we've made.

290
00:49:09,082 --> 00:49:10,692
What unites people?

291
00:49:13,692 --> 00:49:14,712
Armies?

292
00:49:16,602 --> 00:49:17,662
Gold?

293
00:49:20,202 --> 00:49:21,592
Flags?

294
00:49:28,742 --> 00:49:30,022
Stories.

295
00:49:32,842 --> 00:49:35,732
There's nothing in the world more powerful than a good story.

296
00:49:38,172 --> 00:49:39,462
Nothing can stop it.

297
00:49:41,152 --> 00:49:43,092
No enemy can defeat it.

298
00:49:44,772 --> 00:49:46,432
And who has a better story...

299
00:49:47,732 --> 00:49:49,282
than Bran the Broken?

300
00:49:53,292 --> 00:49:56,562
The boy who fell from a high tower and lived.

301
00:49:58,242 --> 00:50:02,102
He knew he'd never walk again, so he learned to fly.

302
00:50:03,252 --> 00:50:05,242
He crossed beyond the Wall,

303
00:50:05,902 --> 00:50:07,072
a crippled boy,

304
00:50:07,412 --> 00:50:09,452
and became the Three-Eyed Raven.

305
00:50:12,392 --> 00:50:13,692
He is our memory,

306
00:50:14,572 --> 00:50:17,102
the keeper of all our stories.

307
00:50:17,342 --> 00:50:21,652
The wars, weddings, births, massacres, famines.

308
00:50:22,112 --> 00:50:23,252
Our triumphs,

309
00:50:24,152 --> 00:50:25,342
our defeats,

310
00:50:26,382 --> 00:50:27,422
our past.

311
00:50:29,392 --> 00:50:32,012
Who better to lead us into the future?

312
00:50:35,402 --> 00:50:38,852
Bran has no interest in ruling and he can't father children.

313
00:50:38,852 --> 00:50:39,792
Good.

314
00:50:40,452 --> 00:50:42,772
Sons of kings can be cruel and stupid,

315
00:50:42,772 --> 00:50:44,322
as you well know.

316
00:50:45,442 --> 00:50:47,422
His will never torment us.

317
00:50:51,652 --> 00:50:54,442
That is the wheel our queen wanted to break.

318
00:51:01,872 --> 00:51:04,662
From now on, rulers will not be born.

319
00:51:05,102 --> 00:51:08,062
They will be chosen on this spot

320
00:51:08,062 --> 00:51:10,602
by the lords and ladies of Westeros...

321
00:51:11,182 --> 00:51:12,742
to serve the realm.

322
00:51:21,292 --> 00:51:23,292
I know you don't want it.

323
00:51:24,492 --> 00:51:27,942
I know you don't care about power.

324
00:51:30,272 --> 00:51:34,012
But I ask you now, if we choose you...

325
00:51:35,702 --> 00:51:37,212
will you wear the crown?

326
00:51:39,072 --> 00:51:41,922
Will you lead the Seven Kingdoms to the best of your abilities

327
00:51:41,922 --> 00:51:44,482
from this day until your last day?

328
00:51:50,562 --> 00:51:52,582
Why do you think I came all this way?

329
00:51:59,962 --> 00:52:02,162
To Brandon of House Stark...

330
00:52:03,542 --> 00:52:04,742
I say aye.

331
00:52:16,522 --> 00:52:17,692
Aye.

332
00:52:24,122 --> 00:52:24,942
Aye.

333
00:52:26,362 --> 00:52:27,222
Aye.

334
00:52:30,552 --> 00:52:31,462
Aye.

335
00:52:34,402 --> 00:52:35,232
Aye.

336
00:52:40,032 --> 00:52:40,812
Aye.

337
00:52:41,792 --> 00:52:42,572
Aye.

338
00:52:43,522 --> 00:52:44,322
Aye.

339
00:52:44,852 --> 00:52:46,582
- Aye. - Aye.

340
00:52:47,072 --> 00:52:47,872
Aye.

341
00:52:50,032 --> 00:52:52,072
I'm not sure I get a vote, but aye.

342
00:52:54,632 --> 00:52:55,372
Aye.

343
00:53:06,882 --> 00:53:09,072
I love you, little brother. I always will.

344
00:53:09,072 --> 00:53:10,392
You'll be a good king.

345
00:53:12,302 --> 00:53:14,532
But tens of thousands of Northmen

346
00:53:14,532 --> 00:53:17,222
fell in the Great War defending all of Westeros.

347
00:53:17,602 --> 00:53:19,352
And those who survived have seen too much

348
00:53:19,352 --> 00:53:21,842
and fought too hard ever to kneel again.

349
00:53:25,282 --> 00:53:27,662
The North will remain an independent kingdom,

350
00:53:28,842 --> 00:53:30,652
as it was for thousands of years.

351
00:53:55,802 --> 00:53:57,812
All hail Bran the Broken, First of His Name,

352
00:54:00,072 --> 00:54:02,352
King of the Andals and the First Men,

353
00:54:03,542 --> 00:54:08,102
Lord of the Six Kingdoms and Protector of the Realm.

354
00:54:10,932 --> 00:54:13,762
All hail Bran the Broken!

355
00:54:25,662 --> 00:54:26,732
Lord Tyrion...

356
00:54:29,052 --> 00:54:30,492
you will be my Hand.

357
00:54:32,442 --> 00:54:35,762
No, Your Grace, I don't want it.

358
00:54:35,802 --> 00:54:37,682
And I don't want to be king.

359
00:54:39,872 --> 00:54:41,452
I don't deserve it.

360
00:54:42,472 --> 00:54:45,322
I thought I was wise, but I wasn't.

361
00:54:45,322 --> 00:54:49,292
I thought I knew what was right, but I didn't.

362
00:54:51,762 --> 00:54:53,332
Choose Ser Davos.

363
00:54:53,402 --> 00:54:54,802
Choose anyone else.

364
00:54:54,802 --> 00:54:56,762
- I choose you. - You cannot.

365
00:54:57,072 --> 00:54:58,152
Yes, I can.

366
00:54:59,002 --> 00:55:01,092
- I'm king. - This man is a criminal.

367
00:55:01,602 --> 00:55:04,102
- He deserves justice. - He just got it.

368
00:55:05,072 --> 00:55:07,062
He's made many terrible mistakes.

369
00:55:07,882 --> 00:55:10,392
He's going to spend the rest of his life fixing them.

370
00:55:15,572 --> 00:55:16,742
It is not enough.

371
00:55:25,562 --> 00:55:28,092
Giving you to the Unsullied would start a war.

372
00:55:29,582 --> 00:55:31,832
Letting you walk free would start a war.

373
00:55:32,872 --> 00:55:34,292
So our new king has chosen

374
00:55:34,292 --> 00:55:36,032
to send you to the Night's Watch.

375
00:55:38,232 --> 00:55:39,722
There's still a Night's Watch?

376
00:55:42,332 --> 00:55:43,582
The world will always need a home

377
00:55:43,592 --> 00:55:45,372
for bastards and broken men.

378
00:55:50,132 --> 00:55:52,132
You shall take no wife,

379
00:55:52,412 --> 00:55:53,602
hold no lands,

380
00:55:54,662 --> 00:55:56,142
father no children.

381
00:55:59,422 --> 00:56:01,462
The Unsullied wanted your head of course,

382
00:56:02,372 --> 00:56:05,532
but Grey Worm has accepted the justice of a life sentence.

383
00:56:07,102 --> 00:56:09,252
Sansa and Arya wanted you freed,

384
00:56:10,632 --> 00:56:13,702
but they understand our new king needs to make peace.

385
00:56:14,582 --> 00:56:16,132
No one is very happy.

386
00:56:17,302 --> 00:56:19,882
Which means it's a good compromise, I suppose.

387
00:56:22,022 --> 00:56:22,972
Was it right?

388
00:56:26,662 --> 00:56:27,672
What I did?

389
00:56:30,942 --> 00:56:32,182
What we did.

390
00:56:36,562 --> 00:56:38,002
It doesn't feel right.

391
00:56:45,342 --> 00:56:47,042
Ask me again in 10 years.

392
00:57:10,172 --> 00:57:12,742
I don't expect we'll ever see each other again.

393
00:57:17,512 --> 00:57:18,932
I wouldn't be so sure.

394
00:57:20,252 --> 00:57:21,652
A few years as Hand of the King

395
00:57:21,652 --> 00:57:24,452
would make anyone want to piss off the edge of the world.

396
00:59:43,692 --> 00:59:45,602
I wish there had been another way.

397
00:59:47,722 --> 00:59:48,882
Can you forgive me?

398
01:00:01,652 --> 01:00:03,652
The North is free, thanks to you.

399
01:00:05,992 --> 01:00:07,372
But they lost their king.

400
01:00:09,662 --> 01:00:11,712
Ned Stark's daughter will speak for them.

401
01:00:14,392 --> 01:00:16,012
She's the best they could ask for.

402
01:00:37,072 --> 01:00:39,722
You can come see me, you know, at Castle Black.

403
01:00:40,962 --> 01:00:42,052
I can't.

404
01:00:42,802 --> 01:00:45,892
You think anyone will dare tell you women aren't allowed?

405
01:00:51,892 --> 01:00:53,432
I'm not going back north.

406
01:00:55,282 --> 01:00:56,452
Where are you going?

407
01:00:58,942 --> 01:01:00,592
What's west of Westeros?

408
01:01:03,482 --> 01:01:04,572
I don't know.

409
01:01:05,282 --> 01:01:06,392
No one knows.

410
01:01:07,682 --> 01:01:09,212
It's where all the maps stop.

411
01:01:11,922 --> 01:01:13,182
That's where I'm going.

412
01:01:22,702 --> 01:01:23,832
You have your Needle?

413
01:01:25,042 --> 01:01:26,102
Right here.

414
01:01:48,432 --> 01:01:49,562
Your Grace.

415
01:01:58,972 --> 01:02:01,212
I'm sorry I wasn't there when you needed me.

416
01:02:03,722 --> 01:02:06,152
You were exactly where you were supposed to be.

417
01:03:19,912 --> 01:03:26,562
担任巴利斯坦·赛尔弥的侍从 随其清剿御林兄弟会
因作战英勇 十六岁时册封为骑士 入选御林铁卫
君临城陷时 在铁王座下杀害国王伊里斯二世
之后被国王劳勃·拜拉席恩一世赦免
由此得到“弑君者”的外号
提利昂·兰尼斯特谋杀了国王乔佛里一世后
侍奉国王托曼一世

418
01:03:45,822 --> 01:03:50,072
被凯特琳夫人释放  立誓找回她的两个女儿
失去了他的...

419
01:04:00,602 --> 01:04:06,762
引诱无垢者进攻凯岩城 为战略大局牺牲家园
诱使坦格利安军队控制高庭
在黄金大道大战中英勇作战 险些葬身龙焰
立誓为生者而战  只身北上临冬城
直面死人军团 于绝境中守卫城堡 直至击败夜王
南下 越狱 试图挽救君临于灭顶之灾

420
01:06:20,212 --> 01:06:21,202
That's not-- Uh--

421
01:06:27,202 --> 01:06:28,252
What's this?

422
01:06:28,332 --> 01:06:30,382
A Song of Ice and Fire.

423
01:06:31,432 --> 01:06:33,112
Archmaester Ebrose's history of the wars

424
01:06:33,112 --> 01:06:34,632
following the death of King Robert.

425
01:06:35,442 --> 01:06:37,422
I helped him with the title.

426
01:06:40,512 --> 01:06:43,192
I suppose I come in for some heavy criticism.

427
01:06:43,722 --> 01:06:45,092
Oh, I wouldn't say that.

428
01:06:45,742 --> 01:06:48,472
Oh, he's kind to me. Never would've guessed.

429
01:06:52,492 --> 01:06:53,562
He's not kind?

430
01:06:55,162 --> 01:06:56,482
- He... - He what?

431
01:06:57,642 --> 01:06:58,942
What does he say about me?

432
01:07:05,182 --> 01:07:08,592
I don't believe you're mentioned, ahem.

433
01:07:30,572 --> 01:07:31,602
- Your Grace. - Your Grace.

434
01:07:31,612 --> 01:07:32,692
- Your Grace. - Your Grace.

435
01:07:51,652 --> 01:07:53,962
We appear to be missing a Master of Whisperers.

436
01:07:54,682 --> 01:07:56,132
And a Master of Laws.

437
01:07:57,132 --> 01:07:59,122
- And a Master of War. - Yes, Your Grace.

438
01:07:59,122 --> 01:08:00,692
Suitable prospects will be brought to you

439
01:08:00,692 --> 01:08:02,392
for an audience in the coming weeks.

440
01:08:04,022 --> 01:08:06,212
And Drogon? Any word?

441
01:08:06,692 --> 01:08:08,732
He was last spotted flying east, toward--

442
01:08:08,732 --> 01:08:10,082
The farther away, the better.

443
01:08:12,102 --> 01:08:13,352
Perhaps I can find him.

444
01:08:14,552 --> 01:08:16,002
Do carry on with the rest.

445
01:08:17,322 --> 01:08:18,832
As you wish, Your Grace.

446
01:08:21,402 --> 01:08:22,412
Ser Podrick.

447
01:08:31,602 --> 01:08:34,172
We serve at your pleasure, King Bran the Broken,

448
01:08:34,342 --> 01:08:37,062
ruler of the Six Kingdoms and Protector of the Realm.

449
01:08:38,002 --> 01:08:40,202
- Long may he reign. - Long may he reign.

450
01:08:40,202 --> 01:08:41,702
- Long may he reign. - Long may he reign.

451
01:08:41,832 --> 01:08:43,012
Long may he reign.

452
01:08:44,842 --> 01:08:46,082
That will improve.

453
01:08:47,262 --> 01:08:48,372
I'm sure it will.

454
01:08:56,542 --> 01:08:58,442
Ser Bronn of the Blackwater,

455
01:08:58,442 --> 01:08:59,712
Lord of Highgarden,

456
01:08:59,712 --> 01:09:02,692
Lord Paramount of the Reach and Master of Coin,

457
01:09:03,822 --> 01:09:06,682
would you say the crown's debt to you has been paid?

458
01:09:06,682 --> 01:09:08,332
In full, my lord Hand.

459
01:09:08,472 --> 01:09:09,522
Good.

460
01:09:09,522 --> 01:09:11,672
Time to start incurring a new one.

461
01:09:11,902 --> 01:09:13,282
We have hungry people to feed.

462
01:09:13,282 --> 01:09:15,082
Can we expect some assistance in this regard?

463
01:09:15,082 --> 01:09:16,212
Indeed we can.

464
01:09:16,812 --> 01:09:19,362
Lord Davos, we have an armada to rebuild and ports to repair.

465
01:09:19,362 --> 01:09:22,732
We have. These projects will begin as soon as

466
01:09:22,732 --> 01:09:26,522
the Master of Coin and Lord of Lofty Titles provides funding.

467
01:09:26,582 --> 01:09:29,312
The Master of Coin looks forward to helping the Master of Ships,

468
01:09:29,312 --> 01:09:32,102
but first he has to ensure we're not wasting coin,

469
01:09:32,152 --> 01:09:34,222
or soon there won't be no more coin.

470
01:09:34,352 --> 01:09:35,142
"Any more."

471
01:09:35,292 --> 01:09:36,532
You Master of Grammar now too?

472
01:09:36,532 --> 01:09:37,612
Grandmaester, ahem,

473
01:09:38,702 --> 01:09:40,992
it is my theory, based on my years of work

474
01:09:40,992 --> 01:09:42,512
on the Casterly Rock sewers,

475
01:09:42,512 --> 01:09:44,842
that clean water leads to a healthier population.

476
01:09:44,852 --> 01:09:47,142
The Archmaester has done some research on this subject

477
01:09:47,142 --> 01:09:48,092
and it turns out--

478
01:09:48,092 --> 01:09:49,902
The strong live and the weak don't.

479
01:09:50,662 --> 01:09:52,932
Find the best builders and set them to the task.

480
01:09:52,932 --> 01:09:55,942
Oh, speaking of builders, all the best brothels burned down.

481
01:09:56,472 --> 01:09:59,422
The Master of Coin is willing to fund reconstruction.

482
01:10:00,022 --> 01:10:02,332
the Archmaester is less than enthusiastic

483
01:10:02,332 --> 01:10:04,562
about the salutary effects of brothels.

484
01:10:04,622 --> 01:10:06,592
Well, I imagine he isn't using them properly.

485
01:10:06,952 --> 01:10:08,762
I think we can all agree that ships

486
01:10:08,762 --> 01:10:10,682
take precedence over brothels.

487
01:10:11,062 --> 01:10:13,332
I think that's a very presumptuous statement.

488
01:10:15,082 --> 01:10:18,492
I once brought a jackass and a honeycomb into a brothel.

